Day 2 Notes: Array, Object, JSON
1. Object {}
Definition

An object is used to store information about one thing using key-value pairs.

Syntax
JavaScript
const employee = {
id: 101,
name: "Lavanya",
role: "Test Engineer"
};
Visualization
Plain Text
employee
│
├── id = 101
├── name = Lavanya
└── role = Test Engineer
When should I use Object?

Use an object when storing information about:

Plain Text
One Employee
One Product
One User
One Manager
One Order
Accessing Values
JavaScript
employee.id

Output:

Plain Text
101
JavaScript
employee.name

Output:

Plain Text
Lavanya
Formula
Plain Text
object.property

Example:

JavaScript
employee.name
2. Array []
Definition

An array is used to store multiple values.

Syntax
JavaScript
const skills = [
"JavaScript",
"Playwright",
"API Testing"
];
Visualization
Plain Text
skills
 
[0] JavaScript
[1] Playwright
[2] API Testing
When should I use Array?

Use an array when storing:

Plain Text
Many Employees
Many Products
Many Skills
Many Orders
Many Users
Accessing Values
JavaScript
skills[0]

Output:

Plain Text
JavaScript
JavaScript
skills[1]

Output:

Plain Text
Playwright
Formula
Plain Text
array[index]

Example:

JavaScript
skills[0]
3. Array of Objects
Definition

Use an array of objects when storing multiple things, and each thing has multiple properties.

Syntax
JavaScript
const employees = [
 
{
id: 101,
name: "Lavanya"
},
 
{
id: 102,
name: "Ram"
}
 
];
Visualization
Plain Text
employees
│
├── Employee 1
│ id = 101
│ name = Lavanya
│
└── Employee 2
id = 102
name = Ram
Why Array?

Because there are:

Plain Text
Many Employees
Why Object?

Because each employee has:

Plain Text
id
name
role
department
Accessing Values

First employee:

JavaScript
employees[0]

First employee name:

JavaScript
employees[0].name

Output:

Plain Text
Lavanya

Second employee:

JavaScript
employees[1].name

Output:

Plain Text
Ram
Formula
Plain Text
array[index].property

Example:

JavaScript
employees[0].name
4. Object Inside Object
Definition

Use an object inside another object when one thing has another single thing inside it.

Example
JavaScript
const employee = {
 
id: 101,
 
name: "Lavanya",
 
manager: {
 
id: 201,
 
name: "Sivakumar"
}
};
Visualization
Plain Text
employee
 
│
├── id
├── name
│
└── manager
│
├── id
└── name
Accessing Values
JavaScript
employee.manager.name

Output:

Plain Text
Sivakumar
Formula
Plain Text
object.object.property
5. Array Inside Object
Definition

Use an array inside an object when one thing contains multiple items.

Example
JavaScript
const employee = {
 
id: 101,
 
name: "Lavanya",
 
skills: [
 
"JavaScript",
 
"Playwright",
 
"API Testing"
]
};
Visualization
Plain Text
employee
 
│
├── id
├── name
│
└── skills
 
[0] JavaScript
[1] Playwright
[2] API Testing
Accessing Values
JavaScript
employee.skills[0]

Output:

Plain Text
JavaScript
Formula
Plain Text
object.array[index]
6. JSON
Full Form
Plain Text
JavaScript Object Notation
Definition

JSON is a data format commonly used by APIs to send and receive data.

Example JSON Response
JSON
{
"employees": [
{
"id": 101,
"name": "Lavanya"
},
{
"id": 102,
"name": "Ram"
}
]
}
Playwright API
JavaScript
const body = await response.json();
============> this JSOn becuase key itself mention with in Double quote 

After conversion:

JavaScript
body

becomes a JavaScript object that you can access using dot notation.

7. How to Identify Array or Object
Starts with {}
JavaScript
{
id: 101,
name: "Lavanya"
}

✅ Object

Starts with []
JavaScript
[
"JavaScript",
"Playwright"
]

✅ Array

Starts with [{ }]
JavaScript
[
{
id: 101,
name: "Lavanya"
}
]

✅ Array of Objects

8. Real API Example
JavaScript
const body = {
 
company: "CTS",
 
employees: [
 
{
id: 101,
name: "Lavanya"
},
 
{
id: 102,
name: "Ram"
}
]
};
Identify Types
JavaScript
body

✅ Object

JavaScript
body.company

✅ String

JavaScript
body.employees

✅ Array

JavaScript
body.employees[0]

✅ Object

JavaScript
body.employees[0].name

✅ String

Output:

Plain Text
Lavanya
Most Important Day 2 Rule
Plain Text
ONE THING
↓
Object {}
 
MANY THINGS
↓
Array []
 
Many Things with Details
↓
Array of Objects
 
[
{},
{},
{}
]
Examples
Plain Text
One Employee
↓
{}
 
Many Employees
↓
[]
 
One Manager
↓
{}
 
Many Skills
↓
[]
 
One Company
↓
{}
 
Company containing Many Employees
↓
{
employees:[]
}
Shortcut for API Automation

Whenever you see API data:

JavaScript
const body = await response.json();

Ask these questions:

Plain Text
1. Is this Object?
2. Which property contains the data?
3. Is that property an Array?
4. Which index do I need?
5. Which property do I need?

Example:

JavaScript
body.employees[0].name

Read it as:

Plain Text
body
↓
employees
↓
first employee
↓
name
↓
Lavanya













